From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] unit: test when binder_voicecall asks for the call list

There was no test for binder_voicecall.c. Run the real thing against
an imitation of the radio service which behaves the way libmtk-ril.so
does: if a getCurrentCalls request finds two held calls, or a held
call and a held conference, the test fails the way the calls did.

The swap is played back in the order seen on the Mindphone. The other
tests cover the ways it can end (error, failed transaction, no response
at all, a late response), the other call control requests, and what must
stay as it was: incoming calls, dial and DTMF don't wait for anything.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
